-- Home life (tenth round): the trash, things that break, and loud neighbors.
-- The trash: cooking, eating and throwing food out fill the kitchen can; renters (Jun, Priya) take the bags to the
-- building's bins any time, Derek puts them in his cart and wheels it to the curb the night before Thursday's pickup
-- (Carl's text m01_carl, Fairview Waste Services' m01_waste). Too many bags at home smell: fruit flies, a note from
-- Carl, the Cedar Street Lofts management or the River Road HOA, then a charge. After the missions something at home
-- breaks now and then (repair rows: where it is reported, what it does until it is fixed, how many days to the visit,
-- what a repair service charges a homeowner): Jun texts Carl, Priya files a request (a notice of entry comes the
-- evening before a weekday visit), Derek calls Riverside Home Services and pays. Late at night a neighbor may be loud
-- (noise rows): four things to do, each with how the night goes. The text and email rows are the engine's messages
-- (n_<what>_<hero>, {name} {thing} {when} {cost} {fee} {order} {day} filled in).
-- The home_events table is in db/schema.sql (this CREATE TABLE is the same).
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS home_events (id varchar(40) PRIMARY KEY, kind varchar(16) NOT NULL, hero varchar(32) NOT NULL DEFAULT 'all', sender varchar(60), title varchar(120) NOT NULL, title_ko varchar(120), body varchar(800) NOT NULL, body_ko varchar(800), place varchar(16), effect varchar(16), cost decimal(8,2), days int, choices json, sort int NOT NULL DEFAULT 0);


